<tei:p><tei:pb n="790" ed="1949 concluding_prayers" facs="https://archive.org/download/PhilipBirnbaumHaSiddurHaShalemTheDailyPrayerBook1949/page/n814_medium.jpg"/><tei:milestone unit="prayer-part" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:tefillah_lishlom_medinat_yisrael/3"/>Remember our brethren, the whole house of Israel, in all the lands of their dispersion. Speedily let them walk upright to Zion thy city, to Jerusalem thy dwelling-place, as it is written in the Torah of thy servant Moses: <tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:deuteronomy/30/4">“Even if you are dispersed in the uttermost parts of the world, from there the Lord your God will gather and fetch you. </tei:seg><tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:deuteronomy/30/5">The Lord your God will bring you into the land which your fathers possessed, and you shall possess it.”</tei:seg><tei:milestone unit="prayer-part"/></tei:p>
